// Optional reference encounters: intersecting/union hubs, capped priority ordering, custom stats,
// counted inventory, flag clearing, arithmetic, conditional effects/diverts and choice fall-through.

=== workshop.hub
@title Expedition Workshop
@hub all(workshop,lesson)
@hub-limit 2

The workshop offers two lessons at a time. Finish one to make room for the next.
When every lesson is done, Tomas will lead you back to camp.

-> camp.hub

=== workshop.packing
@title Pack a trail lunch
@tags workshop,lesson
@priority 20
@once

~ set flag:packing-open
~ give player ration 2

Tomas hands you two rations. One is for the road; the other is lunch.
The inventory counts both, rather than treating a held item as a simple yes/no.

* [Eat one ration] { take player ration; clear flag:packing-open }
-> workshop.packing-done

=== workshop.packing-done
@title Ready to Travel

{if not flag:packing-open and player has ration}
You close the pack with one ration left.
{/if}
The packing flag is now **{flag:packing-open}**.

-> workshop.hub

=== workshop.ledger
@title Balance the expedition ledger
@tags workshop,lesson
@priority 10
@once

~ var:ledger = (6 + 2) * 3 / 2 - 1
~ var:ledger -= 1

The slate reads `((6 + 2) * 3 / 2 - 1) - 1`: **{var:ledger}**.
Tomas checks your arithmetic before trusting you with the expedition accounts.

* [Agree on ten crates] (requires: var:ledger == 10 and var:ledger != 0) -> workshop.hub

=== workshop.identity
@title Sign the expedition register
@tags workshop,lesson
@priority 10
@once

The clerk writes **{player:name#upper}**, then carefully corrects the entry to
{player:name}. The margin says: "{player:pronoun:subject#capitalize} signed
{player:pronoun:possessive} own name; this copy is {player:pronoun:possessive-pronoun}.
Ask {player:pronoun:object} to check it {player:pronoun:reflexive}."

{item:idol#a#capitalize} decorates the clerk's stamp. Its label reads \{expedition copy\}.

> guide: I use {guide:pronoun:subject}/{guide:pronoun:object}. Names matter more than the guild admits.

-> workshop.hub

=== field.hub
@title Field Exercises
@hub any(field,practice)
@hub-limit 1

One exercise remains on the board at a time. The chalk marks disappear as you finish.

-> camp.hub

=== field.resolve
@title Stand your ground
@tags field
@requires not visited(field.resolve)
@priority 10
@once

~ player:courage += 10

You stand still while Tomas crashes through the brush in his least convincing jaguar impression.
Your courage rises to **{player:courage}**, never above its authored maximum of ten.

{if flag:steady}
The courage trigger has marked you **steady**.
{/if}
{if player:courage >= 6}
~ player:xp += 5
{/if}

* [Thank Tomas for the lesson] -> field.hub

=== field.signal
@title Follow the signal
@tags practice
@requires visited(field.resolve) and player:courage >= 6
@once

{if flag:steady}
You follow the whistle without flinching.
-> field.ready
{/if}
-> field.retry

=== field.ready
@title Ready for the Jungle

Both exercises are complete. You have earned a little confidence, not immunity to bad decisions.

-> field.hub

=== field.retry
@title A Second Breath

You need another breath before following the whistle. Tomas waits without comment.

-> field.hub

=== field.bell
@title Test the watch bell
@tags practice
@requires visited(field.ready)
@priority -1
@once

The watch bell has sounded **{var:bell-count}** times. Ring it, silence it, then
ring it again: the trigger counts new alarms, not every moment an alarm stays true.

* [Ring the bell] (requires: not flag:bell-ringing) { set flag:bell-ringing } -> field.bell
* [Silence the bell] (requires: flag:bell-ringing) { clear flag:bell-ringing } -> field.bell
* [Finish the watch drill] { clear flag:bell-ringing } -> field.hub
